=== Text #1 ===
> Ether Capital is a[ Multi-]crypt[ocurrency] Private Portfolio launched the 3rd May of[ 2016] by Bochsler Finance (BF) with[ a] full two-[year track] record.
To achieve its investment goals, Ether[ Capital typically] invested at least 80[%] of its[ total] net assets[ in] large market cap high-yielding cryptocurrencies and initial coin offerings[ (]ICO) of projects which have been approved by Bochsler Finance’s team of experts. Additionally, Ether Capital rebalanced its portfolio on a daily basis to optimize return on investment. This rebalancing effectively guaranteed that we buy low and sell high taking advantage of the volatility in these markets. While the waters of cryptocurrency can be quite turbulent, experience teaches us that–with the right steering and asset diversification–the rewards can be great.
The key risk for[ the fund] is the systemic risk that comes with its full exposure[ to] the cryptocurrency markets – sometimes large systemic downturns cannot be avoided. In such situations, patience is rewarded.
Ether[ Capital] does all the work to get you safely invested in cryptocurrencies.
Growing rate of adoption[. Pro]ven as an[ alternative store of value].[
]Great portfolio diversification strategy. Hedge against traditional financial markets.
With practical applications, the[ value] rises significantly due to the disruptive nature[ of] the blockchain technology[.]
For[ example, without a] bank[,] how[ would] people send money to each other[?
