The[ event] has built up a loyal following over the years and regulars at the Java MTB Challenge use the[ race] to train for the upcoming Wines2Whales and To Hell and Back. Apart from thrilling MTB and trail running across scenic farmland and mountains, the Java MTB Challenge also offers enticing food stalls, good music, wine tasting, lucky draws, prizes to the value of R40,000.00 and a great vibe!
Rout[es] range from a non-technical fun ride which is perfect for families to do together all the way up to gruelling routes for top riders only[.] For safety[ reasons, no] kids under 16 years will be allowed on the 45km and 80[km] tracks[. All] participants will be rewarded with medals and goodie-bags upon crossing that finish line[.]
The 6km MTB[ route] is an easy, non-technical fun ride suitable[ for] small children (parents welcome to ride with[).]
The 20[km route] is ideal[ for] beginners[.] It consists mostly of jeep tracks with some[ single tracks], and is not very technical, with only 250m elevation[. Take] note[ that no] children under 10 years will be allowed the 20 km[ track] and kids younger than 12 years must be accompanied by an[ adult rider.
]The 45[km route] is[ suitable for] intermediate riders with an elevation of about 850m[.
]The 80[km] is a gruelling route for the adrenalin seekers[.] It includes many sections of the 2018 ABSA Cape Epic route as well as virgin territory and custom-built[ single] tracks[.] The 1600m elevation will thrill even the most seasoned rider[.
]Run[ners] can look forward to a 10km vineyard trail run over rugged terrain and crossing the confluence of two rivers[.] The 276m elevation and rocky terrain will be an exciting challenge for novice and experienced[ runners] alike[.
